### ARVDOUL VIBES — PART 1

### Core Experience: Architecture, Interface, Creation, Publishing & Viewing

PART 1 — IMPLEMENTATION SPECIFICATION

Objective: Build the complete foundational Vibes experience for Arvdoul as a production-grade social media feature. This part covers everything required for users to create, publish, view, navigate, manage and control their Vibes.

This is an implementation specification for Firebase AI Studio. It is deliberately restricted to Part 1. Social economy, advanced creator monetization, XP, levels, gifting and advanced creator features belong to subsequent parts.

### 1\. Product definition

Vibes is Arvdoul's ephemeral visual-sharing system, allowing users to publish temporary content that their audience can view through an immersive, full-screen experience.

Vibes must feel like a native component of Arvdoul rather than an independent application embedded inside it.

The experience consists of three primary environments:

* Vibes Feed: Discover and access available Vibes.

* Vibes Viewer: Watch and navigate published Vibes.

* Vibes Studio: Create, edit, preview and publish Vibes.

All three environments must share the existing Arvdoul design system, authentication, profile identity, media infrastructure, navigation and Firebase architecture.

### Core product principles

* Mobile-first, responsive implementation.

* Premium, polished, flagship-native-app-quality UI.

* Consistent light and dark themes.

* Smooth transitions and gesture interactions.

* Fast media loading and reliable playback.

* Privacy-aware publishing.

* Offline-tolerant creation and drafts.

* Accessible controls and understandable interaction patterns.

* Secure Firebase-backed data operations.

* Reusable components and maintainable architecture.

