### 6.3 Playback engine

Create a reliable playback controller.

Image Vibes:

* Use a configurable display duration.

* Default to approximately 5 seconds.

* Pause when the Viewer is not active.

* Resume correctly after interruption.

Video Vibes:

* Use the actual media duration.

* Support playback and pause.

* Respect buffering.

* Avoid advancing while media is buffering.

* Handle media errors.

* Release media resources when no longer needed.

* Avoid unnecessary video preloading.

Text Vibes:

* Use a readable display duration.

* Support manual navigation.

* Avoid excessively short playback for long text.

### 6.4 Progress indicators

Implement segmented progress bars.

Requirements:

* One segment per Vibe in the current sequence.

* Current segment reflects playback progress.

* Previous segments are complete.

* Future segments remain inactive.

* Pause freezes progress.

* Navigation updates progress correctly.

* Buffering does not falsely advance video progress.

* Segment changes do not cause visual flickering.

### 6.5 Navigation logic

Support:

* Next Vibe from the same creator.

* Previous Vibe from the same creator.

* Next creator.

* Previous creator.

* End-of-sequence behavior.

* Deleted Vibe handling.

* Expired Vibe handling.

* Empty sequence handling.

* Reopening a creator's active Vibes.

Do not load every Vibe in the entire application just to navigate between a small number of active Vibes.

### 6.6 Media rendering

Image rendering:

* Preserve aspect ratio.

* Avoid distortion.

* Support portrait and landscape media.

* Use appropriate background treatment.

* Avoid unexpected cropping.

Video rendering:

* Use supported media formats.

* Display a loading indicator.

* Handle autoplay restrictions.

* Handle mute/unmute state where appropriate.

* Avoid playback continuing after navigation.

* Handle interrupted playback.

Text rendering:

* Respect text formatting.

* Support backgrounds.

* Maintain readable contrast.

* Prevent text overflow.

* Support different screen sizes.

### 6.7 Viewer performance

* Preload only nearby content.

* Avoid loading every video simultaneously.

* Release unused media resources.

* Prevent unnecessary component remounting.

* Avoid excessive React state updates during playback.

* Keep progress animation smooth.

* Avoid layout shifts.

* Handle low-memory mobile devices.

